---
description: Explains the active project's workflow file
---

- This project tracks development phase in `{{workflow-file}}`. Treat it as a strict YAML mapping with lowercase keys:
  ```yaml
  phase: <{{#workflow.phase_list}}{{.}}{{^.last}}|{{/.last}}{{/workflow.phase_list}}>
  issue: <optional-dash-delimited-current-work-phrase>
  plan: <optional-plan-document-path>
  tracking: <optional-external-tracker-reference>
  description: <optional-context>
  {{#worktree.linked}}worktree: {{worktree.name}}
  {{/worktree.linked}}
  queue:
    - <optional-queued-issue>
  ```
  `phase` is required. All other fields are optional; omit empty fields. `issue` is a dash-delimited current-work phrase with no spaces and only filesystem-friendly characters. `plan` is a relative path to an existing plan document, not a description. `tracking` is one external tracker string (for example, `UT-441`), never a mapping. Read the exact configured path `{{workflow-file}}` directly; never find it through a glob, repository search, or tracked-file listing, because those can omit dotfiles and ignored files. If it exists, send its complete content with `send_file_content`. If a direct read confirms it is absent, create it to record the current workflow state, using `phase: discussion` when no other phase has been selected, then send its complete content.
